\title{Radioactivity example revisited}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2021-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Recall #{\frac{db}{dt} + k_bb = k_aa_0e^{-k_at}}. Integrating factor #{\mu}: #{\ln\mu = \int^t k_b\,dt = k_bt \Rightarrow \mu = e^{k_bt}}, so}

##{\frac{d}{dt}(e^{k_bt}b) = k_aa_0e^{k_bt - k_at}.}

\p{Consider #{k_a = k_b = k} [the previous P.I. failed]. We have}

##{\frac{d}{dt}(e^{kt}b) = ka_0 \implies e^{kt}b(t) = ka_0t + D \implies b(t) = De^{-kt} + \underbrace{ka_0te^{-kt}}_{\text{a P.I.}}.}

\p{Note: #{te^{-kt}} rather than #{e^{-kt}}.}
